---
# structurer role (qwen) — step 2 of the consolidation loop. Given the problem
# name from step 1, return EXACTLY the items from the list that are variants /
# restatements of it (verbatim, so the caller can remove them from the remaining
# list). The scheme loop guarantees progress even if this returns nothing.
output:
  items(array): string
---
{{role "system"}}
You are a precise analyst. Given an underlying problem and a list of complaints, you return ONLY the complaints from the list that are restatements or variants of that same underlying problem — copied verbatim from the list, nothing invented, nothing reworded.

{{role "user"}}
UNDERLYING PROBLEM:
{{name}}

LIST OF COMPLAINTS:
{{items}}

Return every item from the list that is a variant or restatement of the underlying problem above. Copy each matching item exactly as it appears in the list. If an item is about a different problem, leave it out.
